id:                     E338
trigger_tool:           meson|ctest|g_test|bind|chmod|stat|gsettings
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        test timeout|SIGABRT.*EPERM|mode.*mismatch|socket.*bind|capability.*unsupported
severity:               2
category:               testing, portability, runtime-capability, fail-closed
match_keywords:         capability probe, runtime feature detection, Unix socket bind, POSIX mode preservation, bounded test wait, precise skip
title:                  Gate portability-sensitive tests with production capability probes

root_cause:             Upstream tests often assume that an available API implies the target runtime provides the complete semantic contract. Restricted filesystems can reject bind, chmod, or writes with capability-specific errors, and missing asynchronous backends can leave an event-driven test waiting forever. A shallow API or privilege probe therefore misclassifies an unavailable feature as a product failure and can turn one test into a CI timeout.
affected_scope:        Cross-platform C test suites that exercise optional filesystem, local IPC, permission, or asynchronous notification semantics on sandboxes and embedded targets.
verification_cmd:       Run the exact affected test binaries with their normal harness; require a positive probe before asserting the semantic contract, bound every wait, and record skip only for the classified capability errno or timeout condition.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           probe-before-assert
rec_description:        Implement a small production-path probe that performs the same operation as the test (for example bind a temporary Unix socket or chmod/query a temporary file). Cache the result for the test process, skip only the dependent contract when the probe reports a documented capability errno, and use a finite monotonic deadline for callbacks or traps.
rec_command:            meson test -C build --print-errorlogs glib:fileutils gio:gdbus-peer gio:file gio:gsettings
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               targeted-test-capability-guards

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      preserve-and-report-unknown
fallback_description:   If the probe cannot classify the failure, keep the assertion fail-closed rather than treating an unrelated errno or missing callback as an unsupported feature.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          explicit-error-classification

forbid_1_pattern:       socket\(.*\).*return.*true|uid.*root.*capability|while \(!.*\).*iteration
forbid_1_reason:        Creating a descriptor or inferring capability from uid does not prove bind or semantic permission behavior, and an unbounded event loop can hang the whole CI job.
forbid_1_consequence:   Restricted targets produce false failures or consume the harness timeout without a truthful terminal result.
forbid_2_pattern:       skip.*all|ignore.*errno|increase.*timeout
forbid_2_reason:        Broad skips and larger timeouts hide real regressions and make unsupported behavior indistinguishable from a broken implementation.
forbid_2_consequence:   Tests lose coverage and CI latency increases while genuine failures are masked.

principles:             P002, P006, P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

